fashion is one of the fastest growing  industries on the planet  around the world 80 billion new pieces  of clothing are sold every year  400 more than just 40 years ago  americans alone are buying five times  more garments than in 1980.  now a 1.3 trillion dollar mega industry  fashion employs more than 300 million  people worldwide  while other industries have come a part  of the seams clothing production has  doubled in the last 15 years  but it's a fashion statement with a  steep environmental price tag  making one kilogram of fabric produces  23 kilograms of greenhouse gases  textile production generates more carbon  dioxide than all international flights  and maritime shipping combined  yet half of all clothes are thrown away  within one year  many having never been worn  fashion is now considered the second  most polluting industry in the world  after oil  and with increasing middle classes in  the developing world keen to make their  own fashion statement this will get  worse  if 80 of emerging markets reach western  levels of clothes shopping carbon  dioxide emissions could increase by  nearly 80 percent per person  by 2050  total clothing sales could reach 175  million tons  turning the planet into the biggest  fashion victim of them all  [Music]  you
 

